    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McGovern Estates is delighted to present No. 4 Burnaby Park to the market.\r\n\r\nOccupying a generous site in one of Greystones' most sought-after residential addresses, No. 4 Burnaby Park represents an exceptional opportunity to acquire a substantial detached family home with outstanding potential.\r\n\r\nConstructed in 1973, the property was originally designed with four spacious bedrooms downstairs, two dormer bedrooms upstairs and an additional attic storeroom extending the property to approximately 219.7 sq. m. (2,365 sq. ft.) of well-proportioned accommodation. \r\n\r\nThe home is characterised by bright, open living spaces, with extensive glazing and a multi-aspect orientation allowing natural light to flood the interiors throughout the day.\r\n\r\nSet on a large, mature plot, the property enjoys a spacious and private rear garden, providing an ideal setting for family life, outdoor entertaining and future landscaping opportunities.\r\n\r\nWhilst the property would benefit from modernisation and upgrading, it offers discerning purchasers the rare chance to create a truly exceptional family residence tailored to their own style and requirements.\r\n\r\nWith its unrivalled location, generous accommodation and remarkable scope for enhancement, No. 4 Burnaby Park is a unique offering in today's market. \r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate everything this wonderful home has to offer.\r\n\r\nExtending to 219.7m2 (2,364.83 sq.ft.), the property comprises a porch, entrance hall, open plan living/dining room, kitchen, six bedrooms, one en suite, a family bathroom and guest WC.\r\n\r\nGreystones town is within easy reach where all your needs will be catered for with a wonderful selection of bistros, boutiques, restaurants and shops, the village library, churches and a large number of highly regarded schools. \r\n\r\nA host of sport and leisure clubs abound in the area including sailing, rowing, football, rugby, tennis and GAA. \r\n\r\nThe Shoreline Leisure Centre and swimming pool are located close-by, as are a great choice of renowned golf clubs, including Greystones, Powerscourt and Druids Glen.\r\n\r\nGreystones is situated in a stunning location between the coast and the Wicklow mountains, giving easy access to the local beaches, countryside and nearby villages of Delgany and Enniskerry. \r\n\r\nThe commuter will be delighted at the easy access to local bus stops and the DART station both within walking distance. The N11/M50 is also within easy reach making for an easy commute to the city, airport and beyond.\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION\r\nPorch\r\nTiled flooring, double glazed double doors to entrance hall.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway \r\nCarpeted flooring, carpeted stairs to landing, vaulted ceiling, WC off, double doors to living room.\r\n\r\nLiving Room/Dining Room\r\nCarpeted and laminated wood flooring, open fire, red brick surround, solid wood mantle and tiled hearth, spot lighting, decorative coving, ample glazing with south/west aspect overlooking extensive front lawn. \r\n\r\nKitchen\r\nLaminated wood flooring, fully fitted kitchen, ample countertops, double stainless steel sink unit, large picture window. \r\n\r\nUtility Room\r\nLaminated wood flooring, plumbed for washing machine and dryer, wall based storage units, door to side passage.\r\n\r\nDownstairs WC\r\nLaminated wood flooring, wash hand basin, wall mirror and WC.\r\n\r\nLanding\r\nCarpeted flooring, eaves storage off.\r\n\r\nInner Hallway\r\nCarpeted flooring, large store room and hot press off.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\nCarpeted flooring, floor to ceiling built in wardrobes, mirrored vanity unit, en-suite off.\r\n\r\nEn Suite\r\nLaminated flooring, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, fully tiled shower with mains power shower.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\nCarpeted flooring, floor to ceiling built in wardrobe, overlooking significant rear garden space.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\nCarpeted flooring, floor to ceiling built in wardrobe, overlooking significant rear garden space.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\nCarpeted flooring, floor to ceiling built in wardrobe, overlooking significant rear garden space.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom \r\nWC, pedestal wash hand basin, wall mirror, fully tiled bath unit, telephone hand shower.\r\n\r\nBedroom 5\r\nCarpeted flooring, large gable window overlooking front garden.\r\n\r\nBedroom 6\r\nCarpeted flooring, large gable window overlooking rear garden.\r\n\r\nAttic room\r\nLarge storage space.\r\n\r\nFront Garden\r\nTarmac driveway, grass lawn, covered carport and porch, solid block built boiler shed.\r\n\r\nRear Garden\r\nLarge grass lawn, mature hedging and trees.\r\n\r\nSPECIAL FEATURES\r\nHighly desirable location\r\nOff street parking for 4 plus vehicles\r\nLarge carport \r\nSolid block built boiler shed\r\nExtensive front and rear gardens with grass lawn with mature hedging and planting\r\nOpportunity to extend\r\nWell proportioned rooms\r\nAbundance of natural light\r\n2x large attic rooms\r\nAdditional attic storage room \r\n10 minute walk to Greystones Town\r\nNo management fee\r\nVacant pocession"
      },
